WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.100 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hello today we'll be discussing how to  build a 2 foot tall 4x4 raised bed the  same principles for making this bed can  be used for making raised beds of other  sizes such as 6 by 6 or 4 by 8 the first  step is gathering all the proper  materials there are many types of  materials you can use for building a  raised bed such as wood cinder blocks or  bricks for the structure we will be  building today we have chosen to use  untreated Douglas fir because it is  relatively inexpensive and can last for  many years before showing signs of rot  other useful wood types for building a  raised bed are cedar juniper or  reclaimed wood that has not been treated  we will be building our raised bed two  feet high to make tending to the bed  easy from a seated position if this does  not concern you one foot is plenty high  for a raised bed so in order to build  our structure we have gathered a box of  three inch deck screws or brackets for  reinforcement  a box of finishing washers a cordless  drill for 8 foot 2 by 12 boards and one  8 foot 4x4 if you buy wood from your  local wood supplier or big-box store  they will cut the wood for you you get  started plan read like your raised bed  to go make sure you place it in a spot  that has an even surface and receives  full Sun which is about 8 hours per day  it can be helpful to pre-drill holes so  that the screws go in properly and  easily begin assembling the raised bed  by fastening together two boards the  boards should be flushed together when  building a raised bed it can be very  helpful to have assistants holding the  boards in place we suggest either having  a partner to assist you or a couple of  cinder blocks to hold the board steady  use two screws to fasten the boards  together and repeat this until the first  frame is complete  add the four by fours to each corner  attach the second frame one board at a  time screw the boards to the four by  fours and then to each other  do this until the frame is complete for  even more reinforcement you can add a  bracket to each corner now that the bed  is built fill the inside with cardboard  this will help prevent weeds and will  eventually decompose and become worm  food fill the structure with a gardening  soil and compost blood thank you for  watching this has been a production of  Cornell University on the web at cornell  edu

